:"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1032692?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242","html_url":"https://github.com/arp242","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"88105dc3aca0a5f2ef120e251462ef4c2a957dff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/toml-lang/toml/commits/88105dc3aca0a5f2ef120e251462ef4c2a957dff","html_url":"https://github.com/toml-lang/toml/commit/88105dc3aca0a5f2ef120e251462ef4c2a957dff"}]},{"sha":"b66722dd9c043193ebdcac13e22add62f023a701","node_id":"C_kwDOAH_0UNoAKGI2NjcyMmRkOWMwNDMxOTNlYmRjYWMxM2UyMmFkZDYyZjAyM2E3MDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Martin Tournoij","email":"martin@arp242.net","date":"2026-08-28T19:04:45Z"},"committer":{"name":"Martin Tournoij","email":"martin@arp242.net","date":"2026-09-10T09:59:20Z"},"message":"Clarify Array of Tables do not need to be grouped together\n\nThere was already such a paragraph for tables, so add one for array of\ntables as well.\n\nIn addition, remove the IMHO needless \"The last syntax that has not yet\nbeen described allows\" throat-clearing on the section, and instead of\nclarifying what [[..]] does with JSON,  use TOML inline arrays and\ntables. That removes the need for \"you can also use inline arrays\"\nsection.\n\nFixes #1100","tree":{"sha":"c9c810e1c0d893179747b2c062b8f0b11a002731","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/toml-lang/toml/git/trees/c9c810e1c0d893179747b2c062b8f0b11a002731"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/toml-lang/toml/git/commits/b66722dd9c043193ebdcac13e22add62f023a701","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/toml-lang/toml/commits/b66722dd9c043193ebdcac13e22add62f023a701","html_url":"https://github.com/toml-lang/toml/commit/b66722dd9c043193ebdcac13e22add62f023a701","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/toml-lang/toml/commits/b66722dd9c043193ebdcac13e22add62f023a701/comments","author":{"login":"arp242","id":1032692,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzI2OTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1032692?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242","html_url":"https://github.com/arp242","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"arp242","id":1032692,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzI2OTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1032692?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242","html_url":"https://github.com/arp242","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arp242/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0fad25650176b7bfff4aae262ba4bf847d84533c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/toml-lang/toml/commits/0fad25650176b7bfff4aae262ba4bf847d84533c","html_url":"https://github.com/toml-lang/toml/commit/0fad25650176b7bfff4aae262ba4bf847d84533c"}]}],"files":[{"sha":"771be507e3949b0689ded30cbb875eb38be5f872","filename":"CHANGELOG.md","status":"modified","additions":13,"deletions":0,"changes":13,"blob_url":"https://github.com/toml-lang/toml/blob/b66722dd9c043193ebdcac13e22add62f023a701/CHANGELOG.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/toml-lang/toml/raw/b66722dd9c043193ebdcac13e22add62f023a701/CHANGELOG.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/toml-lang/toml/contents/CHANGELOG.md?ref=b66722dd9c043193ebdcac13e22add62f023a701","patch":"@@ -1,5 +1,18 @@\n # TOML Changelog\n \n+## unreleased\n+\n+- Clarify that comparison for quoted keys is ordinal and doesn't do Unicode\n+  normalization ([#993])\n+\n+- Clarify that tables typically cannot be nested infinitely ([#1087]).\n+\n+- Clarify that arrays of tables do not need to be grouped together ([#1103]).\n+\n+[#993]: https://github.com/toml-lang/toml/pull/993\n+[#1087]: https://github.com/toml-lang/toml/pull/1087\n+[#1103]: https://github.com/toml-lang/toml/pull/1103\n+\n ## 1.1.0 / 2025-12-18\n \n - Allow newlines and trailing commas in inline tables ([#904])."},{"sha":"589ae970c31936356018f883f951c87117ddd7d1","filename":"toml.md","status":"modified","additions":69,"deletions":23,"changes":92,"blob_url":"https://github.com/toml-lang/toml/blob/b66722dd9c043193ebdcac13e22add62f023a701/toml.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/toml-lang/toml/raw/b66722dd9c043193ebdcac13e22add62f023a701/toml.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/toml-lang/toml/contents/toml.md?ref=b66722dd9c043193ebdcac13e22add62f023a701","patch":"@@ -194,6 +194,20 @@ spelling = \"favorite\"\n \"spelling\" = \"favourite\"\n ```\n \n+Quoted keys are considered identical if their code point sequences are the same.\n+It is possible to create distinct keys that appear visually identical. Doing so\n+is discouraged:\n+\n+```toml\n+# VALID BUT DISCOURAGED\n+\n+# prénom = \"Françoise\", using pre-composed LATIN SMALL LETTER E WITH ACUTE (U+00E9, NFC)\n+\"pr\\xe9nom\" = \"Françoise\"\n+\n+# prénom = \"Françoise\", using COMBINING ACUTE ACCENT (U+0301, NFD)\n+\"pre\\u0301nom\" = \"Françoise\"\n+```\n+\n As long as a key hasn't been directly defined, you may still write to it and to\n names within it.\n \n@@ -558,15 +572,15 @@ For the sake of readability, you may replace the T delimiter between date and\n time with a space character (as permitted by RFC 3339 section 5.6).\n \n ```toml\n-odt4 = 1979-05-27 07:32:00Z\n+odt5 = 1979-05-27 07:32:00Z\n ```\n \n One exception to RFC 3339 is permitted: seconds may be omitted, in which case\n `:00` will be assumed. The offset immediately follows the minutes.\n \n ```toml\n-odt5 = 1979-05-27 07:32Z\n-odt6 = 1979-05-27 07:32-07:00\n+odt6 = 1979-05-27 07:32Z\n+odt7 = 1979-05-27 07:32-07:00\n ```\n \n Implementations are required to support at least millisecond precision.\n@@ -590,7 +604,7 @@ ldt3 = 1979-05-27T00:32:00.999999\n Seconds may be omitted, in which case `:00` will be assumed.\n \n ```toml\n-ldt3 = 1979-05-27T07:32\n+ldt4 = 1979-05-27T07:32\n ```\n \n Implementations are required to support at least millisecond precision.\n@@ -623,7 +637,7 @@ lt3 = 00:32:00.999999\n Seconds may be omitted, in which case `:00` will be assumed.\n \n ```toml\n-lt3 = 07:32\n+lt4 = 07:32\n ```\n \n Implementations are required to support at least millisecond precision.\n@@ -705,6 +719,10 @@ In JSON land, that would give you the following structure:\n { \"dog\": { \"tater.man\": { \"type\": { \"name\": \"pug\" } } } }\n ```\n \n+There is no limit on the nesting depth. However, in practice most\n+implementations impose some limit to prevent excessive resource usage and/or\n+crashes. It's recommended to allow at least 100 levels of nesting.\n+\n Whitespace around the key is ignored. However, best practice is to not use any\n extraneous whitespace.\n \n@@ -891,11 +909,11 @@ type.name = \"Nail\"\n \n ## Array of Tables\n \n-The last syntax that has not yet been described allows writing arrays of tables.\n-These can be expressed by using a header with a name in double brackets. The\n-first instance of that header defines the array and its first table element, and\n-each subsequent instance creates and defines a new table element in that array.\n-The tables are inserted into the array in the order encountered.\n+Arrays of tables can be expressed by using a header with a name in double\n+brackets. The first instance of that header defines the array and its first\n+table element, and each subsequent instance creates and defines a new table\n+element in that array. The tables are inserted into the array in the order\n+encountered.\n \n ```toml\n [[product]]\n@@ -911,16 +929,14 @@ sku = 284758393\n color = \"gray\"\n ```\n \n-In JSON land, that would give you the following structure.\n+You can also use inline tables; the following is identical:\n \n-```json\n-{\n-  \"product\": [\n-    { \"name\": \"Hammer\", \"sku\": 738594937 },\n+```toml\n+product = [\n+    { name = \"Hammer\", sku = 738594937 },\n     {},\n-    { \"name\": \"Nail\", \"sku\": 284758393, \"color\": \"gray\" }\n-  ]\n-}\n+    { name = \"Nail\",   sku = 284758393, color = \"gray\" },\n+]\n ```\n \n Any reference to an array of tables points to the most recently defined table\n@@ -949,7 +965,7 @@ name = \"banana\"\n name = \"plantain\"\n ```\n \n-The above TOML maps to the following JSON.\n+The above TOML maps to the following JSON:\n \n ```json\n {\n@@ -1020,12 +1036,42 @@ shape = \"round\"\n color = \"green\"\n ```\n \n-You may also use inline tables where appropriate:\n+Defining arrays of tables out-of-order is discouraged.\n \n ```toml\n-points = [ { x = 1, y = 2, z = 3 },\n-           { x = 7, y = 8, z = 9 },\n-           { x = 2, y = 4, z = 8 } ]\n+# VALID BUT DISCOURAGED\n+[[fruit]]\n+name = \"apple\"\n+\n+[store]\n+name = \"Fruit 'n Veg Emporium\"\n+\n+[[vegetable]]\n+name = \"broccoli\"\n+\n+[[fruit]]\n+name = \"pear\"\n+\n+[[vegetable]]\n+name = \"courgette\"\n+```\n+\n+```toml\n+# RECOMMENDED\n+[store]\n+name = \"Fruit 'n Veg Emporium\"\n+\n+[[fruit]]\n+name = \"apple\"\n+\n+[[fruit]]\n+name = \"pear\"\n+\n+[[vegetable]]\n+name = \"broccoli\"\n+\n+[[vegetable]]\n+name = \"courgette\"\n ```\n \n ## Filename Extension"}]}